␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀-␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀-␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀# Kingsdeep

A long skirmish on 192x192 for you and one ally, made for digging and building - and for trying
new rooms and mechanics mods over many hours.

**You** (House Ember, player 3) start in the south-west in a cavern of rock with gold in its
walls, a heart, a tile of floor round it and imps; **your ally** (House Ashen, player 4) is your
mirror in the south-east. The map is the game's own kind: chambers of rock in undiggable stone,
joined by necks of rock or gold - you dig to everything. Nearest you: a portal, gold seams, a
goblins' den and a henhouse; then a library with a Warlock, a hero post, a training hall, a bile
demon's pit. A river of lava crosses the middle (a few stone bridges; build more); the drowned
west and east are seas whose chambers are islands; far out, secrets walled in undiggable rock -
a vampire's crypt, a fallen angel's temple, the rogues' casino, old baths and a club, a
salamanders' forge. Every other chamber holds something: seams, gems, a pond round an island,
lava, a cave with a neutral or a hero, a mana vault.

**The Crown** (player 5) starts in a great cavern at the top centre: a bare heart and imps, and
round it **King Reginald** (level 10), the Lord of the Land, three princes, the royal guard,
knights and archers. Its computer keeper digs and builds the citadel as the game goes; hero
forts stand on the ways to it. Kill the king's court and break that heart to win.

**Set-up:** turn on Kingsdeep in Options and mods (Bathhouse and Strip Club come with it), pick
`Kingsdeep` on the Skirmish tab, put yourself and House Ashen in **Team 1**, and pick the
Crown's difficulty. With Hero Keeper on, giving the Crown the Heroes side lets its portal bring
heroes too (it starts without one).

```sh
python3 tools/native/run_level.py --level Kingsdeep --skirmish --computer 4 --computer 5 --teams 3+4 --mod kingsdeep
```

**Source:** `source/make.py` writes `source/Kingsdeep.toml` from a BSP layout in the game's own style, by the rules of
[the map guide](../../docs/agents/guides/author-skirmish-maps.md) ("Generated maps"):

```sh
python3 mods/kingsdeep/source/make.py
python3 tools/dk2map/preview.py mods/kingsdeep/source/Kingsdeep.toml .cache/dk2map/kingsdeep.png
python3 tools/dk2map/dk2map.py build mods/kingsdeep/source/Kingsdeep.toml --game "$GAME" --mod mods/bathhouse --mod mods/stripclub --out .cache/dk2map/kingsdeep
```

Checked: the map compiles and loads with the engine, every creature stands on open ground, the
Crown's computer keeper starts building. Not yet checked: a full game to the end, and how
soon the Crown's computer keeper marches south.
title = "Kingsdeep"
description = "A long skirmish for you and one ally: dig and build from a bare heart, find the secrets of the deep, and break King Reginald's citadel in the north. Set yourself and House Ashen to the same team."
kind = "maps"
requires = ["bathhouse", "stripclub"]
[policy]
fix_web_speed = 0
fix_backstab_angle = 0
fix_manufacture_slot = 0
fix_area_damage = 0
title = "Original quirks"
description = "Brings back four bugs of the original: web speed, backstab angle, Workshop slot, blast damage."
kind = "fix"
# The Overseer: a new creature with a mechanic of its own, an aura (mods/README.md, "Auras").
# She is the Mistress's record, art and animations, drawn taller and in blood-red leather; two of
# them may come to every keeper with a Torture Chamber of 16 tiles or more and a Strip Club (the
# Strip Club mod) of 9 or more - with that mod off she does not come.
#
# Whoever of her keeper's creatures is within 3 tiles of her works 40% faster - research,
# manufacture, training, an imp's digging - and grows sour at it (the anger a night in the lair
# clears). She does no work herself but stands where it is done, and takes a place there.

[new_creatures.Overseer]
base = "Mistress"
title = "Overseer"
pool = 2
attraction = [["Torture Chamber", 16], ["Strip Club", 9]]   # rooms (by name) and their tiles; the first is her favourite
tint = 0xD86A5A                   # her colour multiplied by this (0xRRGGBB)
portrait = "gui\\creatures\\evil\\overseer-bg"   # textures/gui_creatures_evil_overseer-bg.png (64x128 in the game's; any 1:2)
icon = "gui\\creatures\\evil\\overseer"         # textures/gui_creatures_evil_overseer.png
scale_percent = 114
hp = 2600                         # the Mistress: 2000
pay = 900                         # ... 600
melee_damage = 520                # ... 480
aura_tiles = 3
aura_work_percent = 40
aura_anger = 40                   # a second; unhappy from about 16000, the lair takes 550 a second off
# Where she goes of her own accord: wherever others work. She has no rate of her own at any of it.
happy_jobs = [[4, 40], [3, 30], [5, 30]]   # training 40%, research 30%, manufacture 30%
hate_job1 = 0                     # the Mistress refuses research and manufacture when set down there;
hate_job2 = 0                     # the Overseer goes where she is put
title = "Overseer"
description = "A new creature: a towering Mistress who drives those near her - they work 40% faster and grow sour."
kind = "content"
