␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀-␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀-␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀# The Velvet Aqueduct

A three-keeper skirmish, 127x127. You are House Velvet in the north; the Brass Foundry holds the
south-west, the Ash Conclave the south-east. The usual skirmish victory: break both enemy hearts
and keep your own.

Every house starts in a cavern of rock with gold in its walls: a heart, a tile of floor round
it and imps. The map is mirrored, chambers of rock in undiggable stone joined by necks of rock or
gold, and you dig to everything. Near every house: a portal, seams, a goblins' den; yours also
has your marble baths (5x5) beside the heart. In the middle the guard island stands in its moat;
west and east the reservoirs are seas of islands; giants keep their pits by the lava in the
northern corners; the old baths and a lost club are walled in rock (a Maiden, a Mistress); the
aqueduct - a river of water with a few bridges - runs between the two enemy houses. Every other
chamber holds something: seams, gems, a pond round an island, a cave with a neutral or a hero.

**Launch from the repository root** (after `tools/native/build.zsh`):

```sh
python3 tools/native/run_level.py --level VelvetAqueduct --skirmish --computer 4 --computer 5 --mod velvet-aqueduct
```

In the game: turn on The Velvet Aqueduct in Options and mods (Bathhouse and Strip Club come on
with it) and pick `VelvetAqueduct` on the Skirmish tab.

**Source:** `source/make.py` writes `source/VelvetAqueduct.toml` from a BSP layout by the rules of
[the map guide](../../docs/agents/guides/author-skirmish-maps.md) ("Generated maps"); change its
seed or its placements, run it, check and build.
title = "The Velvet Aqueduct"
description = "A three-keeper skirmish in the rock: three hearts, a 5x5 bath of yours, everything else dug and built. The drowned guard island, a giant by the lava and the southern aqueduct between the other houses. Turns on Bathhouse and Strip Club."
kind = "maps"
requires = ["bathhouse", "stripclub"]
